    "text": "By Travelyourway Team ,\n7 hours ago LAS VEGAS, NV — The American Civil Liberties Union of Nevada is pressing Clark County School District trustees to step in after the district paused its use of Flock surveillance cameras for investigations. In a letter sent Wednesday, the group said it would be reckless to let school police decide on their own whether to adopt the technology without direct board oversight. Read full article",
